      "title": "Setup and model downloads",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## LTX 2.5 accelerated DFR Diffusion VAE — experimental\n\n1. Accept the LTX 2.5 license and download the split components.\n2. Build the two exact prebaked Q8 DFR page sets from the original development-model Q8 pages.\n3. Put the Diffusion VAE in `ComfyUI/models/vae/`.\n4. Put the Pixel-Spatial IC-LoRA in `ComfyUI/models/loras/LTX-2.5/`.\n5. Run Preflight before generation.\n6. Queue the workflow after Preflight succeeds.\n\nThis workflow keeps exact prebaked DFR sampling and uses the approximate query-tiled Metal neighborhood-attention decoder with a 65,536-row query tile. In a matched 768×512 five-second validation, decode fell from 966.45 to 74.72 seconds and complete-process peak fell from 164.58 to 14.01 GB. The result measured SSIM 0.98763 and PSNR 46.72 dB against the exact Diffusion VAE output. Audio remained identical. Use the practical Conv-VAE workflow when speed and memory matter more than Diffusion VAE detail.\n\n### Downloads\n\n- [LTX 2.5 development transformer, distilled LoRA, and components](https://huggingface.co/Lightricks/LTX-2.5)\n- [Pixel-Spatial IC-LoRA](https://huggingface.co/Lightricks/LTX-2.5-22b-IC-LoRA-Pixel-Spatial-Upscaler)"
      ],
      "color": "#243447",
      "bgcolor": "#15202b"
    },
